+The desktop tray and the dock badge list a session exactly when the sidebar gives it a row (maintainer decision 2026-11-24). One module decides that for both: `list/sidebarSessionTree.ts`. The sidebar's collection (`useSessionProjectCollection`) builds its tree from it: which sessions are listed (`buildSidebarSessionTree`, the known-directory filter and the live gap), how they nest (`nestingParentById`, from `resolveSessionNestingParentId`), and which are nested and so not roots (`collectNestedSessionIds`). The tray (`hooks/useTraySync.ts`) builds the same tree and ownership index from the same stores (`list/sidebarRows.ts`, `readSidebarRowBase`) and asks `resolveSidebarSessionRows` which roots have a row. The attention popover uses the same builder: for the instance on screen from these stores, and for a polled instance from its own answers (`buildSidebarRowBase`), so it lists a session only through a row that instance's sidebar draws (see *Cross-instance attention* in `lib/DOCUMENTATION.md`). A root has one when it is a managed chat (Chats section), when the ownership index places it in a project, worktree or space group, or, failing both, when it is pinned to the default list (Pinned section). The In work and custom sections draw from the project groups, so they add no session of their own. View state stays out: collapsed groups, search, single-project mode and show-more limits hide a row, they do not decide whether it exists.
 
 What this means in the tray:
 
@@ -1929,6 +1929,6 @@ What this means in the tray:
 - A session is nested, and so not a root, when the session it nests under is listed, active or archived. A child of an archived parent therefore has no row of its own while its parent is out of the active list.
 - A project session whose nesting chain loops without reaching a root is listed as a root in its project group (`isInNestingCycle` in `useSessionGrouping`), and the rest of the loop nests under it. The sidebar picks the first member in its own order and the tray the first in tree order, so the loop has one row either way.
 
